ed points coincide:\n   \\(d_{+}=d_{-}=2\\lambda\\). The recurrence (1) then satisfies\n   \\(d_{k+1}=f(d_k)\\le2\\lambda\\) with equality only in the limit.\n   Consequently \\(S_{2k}\\le\\lambda(2k+1)\\) and \\(Q_{2k-1}<2k\\) for all \\(k\\);\n   neither player can force a loss. The maximal strategies give an infinite\n   play, so no player possesses a winning strategy at the critical value.\n\n**Conclusion:**  \nAlice wins exactly when \\(\\lambda>\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\); Bazza wins exactly when\n\\(\\lambda<\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\); and for \\(\\lambda=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\) the game can be\nforced to continue forever.  "
